hnote over WT #LavenderBlush:  WT receives \n peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1_padded_signed_by_boomlet_1_encrypted_by_boomlet_1_for_wt from \n non-initiator Niso, decrypts it \n with wt_privkey, verifies boomlet_1_identity_pubkey's signature. It then derives duress_placeholder by \n separating the padding from \n peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1_padded and sends it to SAR. It also saves \n peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1 for later.
hnote over WT #Lavender:  peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1_padded_signed_by_boomlet_1 := \n decrypt_from_boomlet_1(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_tx_commit", approved_withdrawal_id), \n envelope: peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1_padded_signed_by_boomlet_1_encrypted_by_boomlet_1_for_wt)
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(boomlet_1_identity_pubkey, \n "Boomerang/withdrawal/tx_commit_envelope", peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1_padded_signed_by_boomlet_1) == \n True
hnote over WT #Lavender:  peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1_padded := \n peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1_padded_signed_by_boomlet_1.content \n duress_placeholder := peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1_padded.padding \n peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1 := peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1_padded.content

' Step 42
WT o-> SAR:  <b>WithdrawalNonInitiatorWtSarMessage1[=WithdrawalWtSarMessage1] \n duress_placeholder \n boomlet_1_identity_pubkey \n approved_withdrawal_id
hnote over SAR #LavenderBlush:  SAR receives {duress_placeholder, boomlet_1_identity_pubkey, \n approved_withdrawal_id} from WT. It decrypts duress_placeholder using the Boomlet-to-SAR CBC/CMAC envelope \n context and sar_privkey to get duress_placeholder_plaintext. It classifies the plaintext as valid safe if it is all-zero \n 32-byte padding, valid duress if its derived doxing_data_identifier exists, \n or malformed otherwise. If it was valid duress and the tuple of approved_withdrawal_id, the received \n boomlet_1_identity_pubkey, and envelope IV of duress_placeholder was not previously saved, \n SAR activates duress response, uses duress_placeholder_plaintext as doxing_key_for_sar to decrypt \n static_doxing_data_encrypted_by_doxing_key_for_sar, derives device_data_key from doxing_key_for_sar for each retained upload, \n derives dynamic_doxing_data_cbc_cmac_keys from device_data_key, \n decrypts each retained upload's dynamic_doxing_data_encrypted_by_device_data_key with \n dynamic_doxing_data_cbc_cmac_keys, and makes every retained upload available to SEARCH AND RESCUE. \n For valid safe or duress placeholders, SAR signs duress_placeholder with sar_privkey and encrypts it with \n boomlet_1_identity_pubkey. Malformed placeholders are rejected before any acknowledgment is created.
hnote over SAR #Lavender:  duress_placeholder_plaintext := decrypt_from_boomlet_1(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_duress_placeholder", approved_withdrawal_id), \n envelope: duress_placeholder)
hnote over SAR #Lavender:  is_safe_placeholder := (duress_placeholder_plaintext == zero_bytes_32) \n derived_doxing_data_identifier := tagged_sha256("Boomerang/doxing_data_identifier", \n duress_placeholder_plaintext) \n is_valid_duress_placeholder := (!is_safe_placeholder && sar_record_exists(derived_doxing_data_identifier))
hnote over SAR #Pink:  Assert is_safe_placeholder || is_valid_duress_placeholder
opt #LightBlue SEARCH AND RESCUE [is_valid_duress_placeholder and (approved_withdrawal_id, \n boomlet_identity_pubkey, duress_placeholder.iv) not previously saved]
hnote over SAR #Lavender:  doxing_data_identifier := derived_doxing_data_identifier \n doxing_key_for_sar := duress_placeholder_plaintext \n static_doxing_data := cbc_cmac_decrypt(keys: derive_cbc_cmac_keys(doxing_key_for_sar, \n "Boomerang/sar_stored_data"), context: canonical_encode("Boomerang", PROTOCOL_VERSION, "sar_static_data", doxing_data_identifier), envelope: \n static_doxing_data_encrypted_by_doxing_key_for_sar) \n retained_dynamic_doxing_data_uploads := all_retained_uploads(doxing_data_identifier) \n dynamic_doxing_data_history := [] \n for each retained_dynamic_doxing_data_upload in retained_dynamic_doxing_data_uploads: \n   device_data_key := kdf_counter_cmac_aes256(doxing_key_for_sar, \n   "Boomerang/sar_dynamic_device_data_key/v1", \n   canonical_encode(retained_dynamic_doxing_data_upload.device_id), 32) \n   dynamic_doxing_data_cbc_cmac_keys := derive_cbc_cmac_keys(device_data_key, "Boomerang/sar_stored_data") \n   dynamic_doxing_data := cbc_cmac_decrypt(keys: dynamic_doxing_data_cbc_cmac_keys, \n   context: canonical_encode("Boomerang", PROTOCOL_VERSION, "sar_dynamic_data", doxing_data_identifier, \n   retained_dynamic_doxing_data_upload.device_id, retained_dynamic_doxing_data_upload.upload_id, \n   retained_dynamic_doxing_data_upload.upload_seq_num), \n   envelope: retained_dynamic_doxing_data_upload.dynamic_doxing_data_encrypted_by_device_data_key) \n   dynamic_doxing_data_history.append(dynamic_doxing_data) \n end for \n save(approved_withdrawal_id, boomlet_1_identity_pubkey, duress_placeholder.iv) \n Enter SEARCH_AND_RESCUE_MODE
end
hnote over SAR #Lavender:  duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar := sign_message(sar_privkey, \n "Boomerang/withdrawal/sar_placeholder_response", duress_placeholder) \n duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_1 := encrypt_for_boomlet_1(context: canonical_encode("withdrawal_sar_placeholder_response", approved_withdrawal_id), \n content: duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar)

' Step 43
SAR o-> WT:  <b>WithdrawalNonInitiatorSarWtMessage1 \n duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_1
hnote over WT #LavenderBlush:  WT receives duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_1 \n from SAR and continues processing peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1. \n It verifies boomlet_1_identity_pubkey's signature on peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1, checks \n approved_withdrawal_id to be the one \n expected and event_block_height to be fresh. WT then signs peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1 with \n wt_privkey. WT then sends the \n collection of peer_i_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_i_signed_by_wt [0 <= i <= 4] to Each Niso alongside its \n respective \n duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_i.
hnote over WT #Lavender:  most_work_bitcoin_block_height := rpc_client.get_block_height()
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert verify_signature(boomlet_1_identity_pubkey, "Boomerang/withdrawal/tx_commit", \n peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1) == True
hnote over WT #Lavender:  peer_1_tx_commit := peer_1_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_1.content
hnote over WT #Pink:  Assert peer_1_tx_commit.approved_withdrawal_id == approved_withdrawal_id
hnote over WT #Pink:  <b>Freshness check \n Assert peer_1_tx_commit.event_block_height >= (most_work_bitcoin_block_height - \n TOLERANCE_IN_BLOCKS_FROM_TX_COMMITMENT_BY_NON_INITIATOR_PEER_TO_RECEIVING_NON_INITIATOR_PEERS_TX_COMMITMENT_BY_WT_HAVING_SAR_RESPONSE_BACK_TO_WT) \n Assert peer_1_tx_commit.event_block_height <= most_work_bitcoin_block_height

' Step 44
WT o-> Non_Initiator_Peers:  <b>WithdrawalWtNonInitiatorNisoMessage4 \n Collection<peer_i_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_i_signed_by_wt> [0 <= i <= 4] \n duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_i [2 <= i <= 4]
autonumber 44 "<b>[00]"

' Step 44
WT o-> Niso:  <b>WithdrawalWtNonInitiatorNisoMessage4 \n Collection<peer_i_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_i_signed_by_wt> [0 <= i <= 4] \n duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_1
autonumber 44 "<b>[00]"

' Step 44
WT o-> Initiator_Peer: <b>WithdrawalWtNisoMessage2[=WithdrawalWtNonInitiatorNisoMessage4] \n Collection<peer_i_tx_commit_signed_by_boomlet_i_signed_by_wt> [0 <= i <= 4] \n duress_placeholder_signed_by_sar_encrypted_by_sar_for_boomlet_0

note over User, SAR #Cyan:  From this point on, non-initiator follows the same steps as initiator. (Withdrawal \n Diagram)
@endpuml
